`a` is a square array of `double` in C (row-major), with 10,000 rows and columns; N denotes the side length. Assume 8-byte doubles, 64-byte cache lines, a matrix larger than cache, and no compiler loop interchange. Which loop has better sequential locality?

```c
/* A: adjacent columns in one row. */
for (i = 0; i < N; i++)
  for (j = 0; j < N; j++)
    s += a[i][j];

/* B: same column in successive rows. */
for (j = 0; j < N; j++)
  for (i = 0; i < N; i++)
    s += a[i][j];
```
